    "body": "# Universal Checkpointing: read AutoEP ZeRO-3 optimizer files one at a time\n\n<!-- r3 2026-10-15, new PR. Branch peng-fix-ucp-stream-expert-states-v1 (worktree\n/fsx/peng/workspace/ds-fix-ucp-stream-expert-states) on master 5f266e26d; `deepspeed/checkpoint/ds_to_universal.py`,\n+16 -8 lines. Round-1 text: descriptions/ucp-stream-expert-states.md. -->\n\n\n## Problem\n\n`ds_to_universal` converts a ZeRO-3 AutoEP checkpoint in two parts. The dense parameters go through the usual\nextract-and-merge path, which reads one optimizer file per worker and writes fragments to `tmp/`. The routed experts\ngo through `_consolidate_zero3_autoep_expert_states`, which first loads **every** rank's optimizer file into one dict\n(`optim_states_by_rank`) and then keeps a copy of every expert fragment in memory until all of them are merged.\n\nTogether those files hold every optimizer state of the model: fp32 (or bf16) master weights plus both Adam moments.\nFor a large MoE model that is more than one host has:\n\n| Model | Parameters | Optimizer state, fp32 master + fp32 Adam (12 B/param) | bf16 master + bf16 Adam (6 B/param) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MiniMax-M3 | 426.2B | 4.65 TiB | 2.33 TiB |\n| GLM-5.2 | 743.4B | 8.11 TiB | 4.06 TiB |\n\nThe H200 nodes this was found on have 2 TiB of host memory, so the conversion cannot finish for either model.\n\n## Change\n\n`_consolidate_zero3_autoep_expert_states` reads one rank's optimizer file at a time. Each expert fragment it finds is\nwritten to `<output>/tmp/autoep_expert_fragments/` (one file per parameter, optimizer state, EP rank and partition\nrank) and the rank's file is released before the next one is read. The merge then loads, for one parameter and one\nstate at a time, only that parameter's fragments. Peak host memory becomes one optimizer file plus one full expert\ntensor, instead of all optimizer files.\n\nThe checks are unchanged: missing ranks, duplicate or missing expert-data-parallel partitions, shape mismatches and\nplacement disagreements raise the same errors. The temporary fragments live under `<output>/tmp`, which the converter\nalready uses for the dense fragments and removes at the end.\n\n## Tests\n\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/checkpoint/test_autoep_affine_universal.py` (calls the function directly; CPU) | 20 passed (master 1c862f7df + this change); master 5f266e26d + this change, both files together: 63 passed |\n| `tests/unit/v1/moe/test_autoep_checkpoint.py` (AutoEP ZeRO-3 save, convert, load at other layouts; GPU) | 43 passed |\n\nHardware for the GPU tests: 1 node of 8 H200 (driver 580.126.09), torch 2.8.0+cu126, pytest 9.1.1.\n`pre-commit run --files` passes on the changed file.\n\nNot measured: the peak host memory of a full-size conversion before and after. The bound follows from the code:\nbefore, every rank's optimizer file is loaded at once (for MiniMax-M3 with fp32 master weights and fp32 Adam states,\n4.65 TiB in total, more than the 2 TiB of the H200 hosts this was found on); after, one rank's file plus one\nparameter's fragments.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nSearched open and recent pull requests on 2026-10-15 (\"universal checkpoint\", \"ds_to_universal\", \"AutoEP\ncheckpoint\"): #8800 plans live expert transfers between placements and #8637 links ZeRO-1/2 fragments; neither\nchanges how `ds_to_universal` reads the ZeRO-3 AutoEP optimizer files.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n| Cell | Validated |\n|---|---|\n| ZeRO-3 + AutoEP checkpoint conversion, save / convert / load at other layouts | yes (tests) |\n| Dense (non-AutoEP) ZeRO-3 conversion | path unchanged |\n| ZeRO-1 / ZeRO-2 conversion | path unchanged |\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis change, its tests and this description were prepared with AI assistance (Claude).\n",
